meta {
  name: Upload Document To S3 (PUT)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

put {
  url: {{documentUploadUrl}}
  body: file
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/pdf
}

body:file {
  @file:
}

docs {
  Step 2 of 3 — PUT the document file directly to S3 using the pre-signed URL.

  IMPORTANT:
  - auth must be "none" — the presigned URL already contains AWS credentials in its query params.
  - Content-Type must exactly match what was sent to the presign endpoint.
  - Do NOT paste the URL manually — {{documentUploadUrl}} is captured automatically by
    presign-document.bru.

  Setup:
  1. Run presign-document first — it sets {{documentUploadUrl}} in the environment
  2. Click the body field and select your file
  3. Run this request — expect HTTP 200 (no body) from S3
  4. Run verify-document to confirm and get the permanent URL
}
